cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use repository-authored InclusiveShift-HAR software, cite this
  metadata and cite every third-party dataset separately under its own terms.
title: >-
  InclusiveShift-HAR: An Auditable Participant-Exclusive Benchmark for
  Ability-Associated Population Shift in Smartphone Activity Recognition
type: software
version: 0.1.6a0
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
abstract: >-
  Research software for auditable, participant-exclusive released-block
  evaluation of ability-associated population shift in smartphone inertial
  human activity recognition. The released cohort label is not a direct measure
  of physical ability, and InclusiveHAR v4 trial boundaries are unrecoverable.
  The locked ten-participant target evaluation found compact DANN and CORAL
  effectively tied, while the full MoRe-HAR configuration scored lower on both
  mean and lower-tail participant macro-F1.
keywords:
  - human activity recognition
  - wearable sensing
  - inertial sensors
  - domain generalization
  - participant-exclusive evaluation
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
notes: >-
  Apache-2.0 applies only to repository-authored material that the copyright
  holder has authority to license. Third-party datasets, legacy coursework
  artifacts, checkpoints, papers, and figures retain their original terms.
